About
-----

OpenMarinkaRodeo is a GPL licensed SIP server implementation. It started as a fork of
Fokus Fraunhofer SIP Express Router (SER) project. OpenMarinkaRodeo wants to be a more
open project, not only from license point of view, but more open as project
management, especially for external contributions.

OpenMarinkaRodeo wants to overcome the development latency of current SER project,
to ensure a shorter path into a release for new added features.
OpenMarinkaRodeo is a project maintained by OpenMarinkaRodeo Solutions
           http://www.openMarinkaRodeo-solutions.com/
by a team including core and main developers of SER project.


Info
----

For information regarding the OpenMarinkaRodeo installation, please see the INSTALL 
file.

For current developers/contributors of this project, see the CREDITS and
AUTHORS file. For complete license information, please see the COPYING file.
For an overview of OpenMarinkaRodeo modules, see this listing on openMarinkaRodeo.org:
	https://www.openMarinkaRodeo.org/Documentation/Modules


Docs
----

Documentation about each module can be found in the README file in each
module directory. For online documentation, please see
           https://openMarinkaRodeo.org/Resources/Documentation

For additional documentation, tutorials and examples please see also
           https://openMarinkaRodeo.org/Resources/DocsTutorials



Questions
---------

For any question related to the OpenMarinkaRodeo usage, please use the
           users@lists.openMarinkaRodeo.org
public mailing list.

For questions regarding the development of OpenMarinkaRodeo - like contributions, bug
reports, etc - please use the
           devel@lists.openMarinkaRodeo.org
public mailing list.

For questions regarding businesses around OpenMarinkaRodeo - like products,
consultancy, trainings, etc - please use the
           business@lists.openMarinkaRodeo.org
public mailing list.

Also there is a generic news mailing list where you can learn about what is
new or important for the OpenMarinkaRodeo project, about alerts and updates regarding
relaces and about events around the project.
           news@lists.openMarinkaRodeo.org
